# Q2. Profit/Loss for 100 Units

```javascript
let cp = Number(prompt("Enter Cost Price (CP):"));
let sp = Number(prompt("Enter Selling Price (SP):"));

let quantity = 100;

if (sp > cp) {
    let profitPerUnit = sp - cp;
    let totalProfit = profitPerUnit * quantity;

    console.log("Profit per unit = " + profitPerUnit + "₹");
    console.log("Total Profit on 100 units = " + totalProfit + "₹");

} else if (sp < cp) {
    let lossPerUnit = cp - sp;
    let totalLoss = lossPerUnit * quantity;

    console.log("Loss per unit = " + lossPerUnit + "₹");
    console.log("Total Loss on 100 units = " + totalLoss + "₹");

} else {
    console.log("No Profit No Loss");
}
```

### Input

```text
CP = 50
SP = 60
```

### Output

```text
Profit per unit = 10₹
Total Profit on 100 units = 1000₹
```

If:

```text
CP = 50
SP = 45
```

Output:

```text
Loss per unit = 5₹
Total Loss on 100 units = 500₹
```

